# Agent Workflow

Rules for Cursor agents. Entry index: `AGENTS.md`.

## Modes

| Mode | Agent may | Agent must not |
|------|-----------|----------------|
| Ask | Read, search, explain | Edit files, implement |
| Plan | Refine plans, commit lists | Implement code |
| Agent | Execute agreed plan | Edit without plan agreement |

## Verify before claiming

Read or search the repo before stating how code, APIs, or paths work. Run commands when possible. Never fabricate paths, flags, or test results.

### Pre-edit checklist

1. Search for existing helpers — extend before inventing.
2. Read `pyproject.toml` for established dependencies.
3. Confirm paths with glob/read — never assume layout from memory.
4. Name the architecture layer before implementing (see `architecture.mdc`).

## Merge authorization

Agents **must not** `git commit`, `git push`, or open a PR unless the user explicitly asks in the **current task**.

## Scope

- Keep changes tied to the requested scope.
- After ~20 file edits: short status update.
- One plan chunk per session unless user expands scope.
